    stEv_open:'App opened',stEv_ob_step:'Sign-up step',stEv_ob_done:'Sign-up finished',stEv_guest_start:'Guest start',stEv_login:'Account sign-in',stEv_plan_created:'Plan created',stEv_bilan_done:'Session logged',stEv_morning_check:'Morning check',stEv_adapt_vdot:'VDOT accepted',stEv_share_open:'Share image opened',stEv_share_image:'Image shared',stEv_races_open:'Race calendar',stEv_race_ics:'Race added to calendar',stEv_race_propose:'Race suggested',stEv_method_open:'Method page',stEv_weather_location:'Weather place set',stEv_ramadan_set:'Ramadan setting',stEv_install_open:'Install guide',stEv_install_accepted:'Install accepted',stEv_install_done:'App installed',stEv_export_data:'Data export',stEv_import_data:'Data import',
    
    anTitle:'Anonymous statistics',anDesc:'Helps improve IKORUN: which features are used, on which phones. A random ID, never your account, sessions or location.',anOnToast:'Anonymous statistics on',anOffToast:'Statistics off: nothing will be sent',stTitle:'App statistics',stNotAdmin:'Reserved for the app administrator.',stDays:{one:'{0} day',other:'{0} days'},stToday:'Active today',stWau:'Active, 7 days',stMau:'Active, 30 days',stInstalled:'App installed',stOfActive:'of {0} active',stDauTitle:'Active per day',stDauChart:'Number of active installs each day',stFunnel:'Funnel',stF_open:'Opened the app',stF_ob_done:'Finished sign-up',stF_plan_created:'Created a plan',stF_bilan_done:'Logged a session',stRetention:'Retention',stCohort:'{0} of {1}',stRetentionNote:'Share of new installs that came back exactly 1, 7 or 30 days after their first day (new in the last 90 days).',stFeatures:'Features used',stUsers:{one:'{0} person',other:'{0} people'},stNone:'No data yet for this period.',stLangs:'Languages',stPlatforms:'Platforms',stDesktop:'Computer',stOther:'Other',stVersions:'Versions (last 7 days)',stPrivacyNote:'Anonymous figures: one random ID per install, not linked to accounts. People who refuse statistics don’t appear.',stCfNote:'Site visits: Cloudflare Web Analytics dashboard.',mtTitle:'The IKORUN method',mtIntro:'Your plan isn’t random: it follows published rules used by coaches, applied on your phone from your times and your session logs. Here they are, with their limits.',mtH_level:'Your level: VDOT',mtP_level:'Your best recent time (5K, 10K, half…) gives a fitness index, Jack Daniels’ VDOT. It sets all your paces. It goes up when you run faster than planned at the same effort (at least 2 of 3 quality sessions), and it is lowered after a break, following the loss measured by Daniels: nothing before 5 days, about 3% at 2 weeks, 7% at 4 weeks.',mtH_zones:'Paces',mtP_zones:'Each session targets a precise zone of your maximal aerobic speed (vVO2max): easy around 70%, threshold around 88%, long intervals around 98%, short intervals around 105%. Most of your volume stays easy: that’s what builds fitness without breaking you. The app checks that distance × pace = duration for every session.',mtH_structure:'How the plan is built',mtP_structure:'The plan is built backwards from race day: general preparation, aerobic development, specific development, peak, then taper. One week in four is lighter (at most 80% of the biggest week) so your body absorbs the work. The long run stays the longest session of the week.',mtH_load:'Load, without excess',mtP_load:'Volume rises by at most 10% a week, never two hard sessions in a row, at most two very hard sessions a week. The app compares your load over the last 7 days with the last 4 weeks (acute:chronic ratio): above 1.3 two mornings in a row, the next 3 days are 15% lighter; above 1.5, the following week is 30% lighter and hard sessions become easy.',mtH_adapt:'What changes your plan',mtP_adapt:'After each log: perceived effort (RPE) compared with the expected one, pace compared with the target, accounting for heat, wind, hills and fasting. Pain of 4/10 or more, or a limp, means 3 days without running; the same pain 3 times in a week blocks hard sessions and advises you to see a professional. A missed session is moved within the week or dropped, never made up by doubling. Every change is explained and can be undone.',mtH_heat:'Heat',mtP_heat:'When it’s hot and humid, the same pace costs more. IKORUN adds temperature and dew point (in °F) and applies Mark Hadley’s table: nothing up to 100, then up to 10% slower pace; above 180, no hard session. Forecasts come from Open-Meteo.',mtH_ramadan:'Ramadan',mtP_ramadan:'If you turn it on, volume drops by 10, 20 or 30% during the month, the most intense sessions become threshold work, and hard sessions are placed after iftar. After Eid, two return weeks (−10% then −5%) bring you back to your usual volume.',mtH_limits:'Limits',mtP_limits:'IKORUN is not medical advice. Lasting pain, feeling unwell, palpitations: stop and see a doctor. The rules work for most runners, not all: if a session feels too hard, say so in the log and the plan adjusts. Before returning to sport after a health problem, ask a doctor.',mtSamples:'Sample plans',mtSamplesLead:'Generated by the same engine as your plan, for typical profiles. Print them or save as PDF.',mtWeeksShort:'wk',mtS_s5k:'5K · beginner',mtS_s10k:'10K · intermediate',mtS_sSemi:'Half marathon · intermediate',mtS_sMar:'Marathon · advanced',mtSampleSub:{one:'{0} session a week · VDOT {1}',other:'{0} sessions a week · VDOT {1}'},mtSampleVol:'starting volume {0} to {1} km a week',mtSampleNote:'Example for a runner with no history in the app. Your own plan starts from your times, your available days and what you have already run.',mtValid:{zero:'Automatic plan check: no errors.',one:'Automatic plan check: {0} error.',other:'Automatic plan check: {0} errors.'},mtPrint:'Print or PDF',mtBack:'The method',mtWeek:'Wk',mtDeload:'lighter',mtPaces:'Paces for this profile',mtZone_E:'Easy',mtZone_M:'Marathon pace',mtZone_T:'Threshold',mtZone_I:'Long intervals',mtZone_R:'Short intervals',mtSources:'Sources',mtSrc_daniels:'Jack Daniels, <i>Daniels’ Running Formula</i>, 3rd ed., Human Kinetics, 2013: VDOT, pace zones, fitness loss after a break.',mtSrc_seiler:'S. Seiler, “What is best practice for training intensity and duration distribution in endurance athletes?”, <i>Int J Sports Physiol Perform</i> 5(3), 2010: most volume at easy intensity.',mtSrc_gabbett:'T. Gabbett, “The training–injury prevention paradox”, <i>Br J Sports Med</i> 50, 2016: acute:chronic workload ratio.',mtSrc_foster:'C. Foster, “Monitoring training in athletes with reference to overtraining syndrome”, <i>Med Sci Sports Exerc</i> 30(7), 1998: session-RPE load, monotony.',mtSrc_hadley:'Mark Hadley’s table (temperature + dew point in °F) for adjusting pace to heat.',mtSrc_ramadan:'A. Chaouachi et al., “Effects of Ramadan intermittent fasting on sports performance and training: a review”, <i>Int J Sports Physiol Perform</i> 4(4), 2009.',mtNoAi:'No artificial intelligence: all these rules are written in the app and computed on your phone.',mtLink:'How your plan is built',
    
